{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.weight_denominator_vanishes_at_monodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.weight_denominator_vanishes_at_monodromy","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L109-L118","doc":"**The monodromy point is singular**: the weight denominator vanishes at\nthe T2 Hecke evaluation `q = i`. The Markov weights have a genuine pole at\nthe monodromy point — value transport is anchored at `q = 1`, module\nstructure at `q = i`; complementary, never interchangeable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.den_in_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.den_in_q","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L104-L107","doc":"The Wenzl-variable denominator is the q-variable denominator at `q = s²`:\nthe two presentations agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.denominator_factors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.denominator_factors","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L99-L102","doc":"The weight denominator in the q-variable factors — over ANY commutative\nring (§7c-generic): `q³+q²+q+1 = (q+1)(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.anchor_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.anchor_forced","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L82-L97","doc":"**The anchor is forced**: on `s > 0`, the canonical weight matches the\nChevalley–Weil dimension fraction `3/4` exactly at `s = 1` and nowhere else.\nThe transport point is derived, not chosen. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.quintic_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.quintic_pos","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L79-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.matching_factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.matching_factorization","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L72-L77","doc":"The exact factorization behind the forced anchor:\n`4·num − 3·den = −(s−1)·(quintic)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.y11_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.y11_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L68-L70","doc":"Value identity, antisymmetric channel: `y₁₁(1) = 1/4` — the T1 invariant\ndimension 1 over the genus g = 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.y2_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.y2_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L64-L66","doc":"Value identity, symmetric channel: `y₂(1) = 3/4` — the T1 Chevalley–Weil\nmoving dimension 3 over the genus g = 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.weights_normalized","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.weights_normalized","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L58-L62","doc":"The weights are normalized: `y₂ + y₁₁ = 1` identically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.den_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.den_pos","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.y11","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.y11","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L52-L54","doc":"Canonical H₂ Jones–Markov weight of the antisymmetric channel `λ = [1,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.y2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport.y2","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovWeightValueTransport.lean#L48-L50","doc":"Canonical H₂ Jones–Markov weight of the symmetric channel `λ = [2]`,\nin the Wenzl variable `s = √q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}